          answer: `
<p>Filter at the server — the LLM should never receive 200 unranked items to sift through.</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Add a limit parameter.</strong> Expose <code>{ "limit": { "type": "number", "default": 10 } }</code> in the Tool's inputSchema. The LLM then requests a reasonable slice instead of everything at once.</li>
  <li><strong>Rank results server-side before returning.</strong> A "red widget" query should return the 10 best matches ordered by relevance — not 200 results in insertion order. A database query with ORDER BY can rank; the LLM cannot.</li>
  <li><strong>Consider switching to a Resource.</strong> If agents need the full catalog for context rather than for search, expose <code>product://catalog</code> as a Resource with a server-side LIMIT 500. They read it once at conversation start instead of re-fetching on every turn.</li>
</ol>
<p>Rule of thumb: never ask the LLM to filter a large list. A WHERE clause is faster, cheaper, and more accurate.</p>
