<p>Two tests help you decide.</p>
<p><strong>The timing test</strong> — can you precompute the result before the conversation starts?</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Yes → Resource.</strong> Product catalog, pricing rules, shipping zones — the content is the same regardless of what the agent knows right now. Expose it as a URI and let agents read it once for context.</li>
  <li><strong>No → Tool.</strong> <code>get_order_status(order_id)</code> where the ID was discovered during the conversation. <code>check_inventory(sku)</code> where the SKU came from what the customer just said. These depend on runtime state and must be called with specific parameters.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>The cost of getting it wrong:</strong> Tool for static data means a redundant DB query on every call, each burning unnecessary tokens. Resource for dynamic data means stale results that don't reflect what the agent actually needs right now.</p>
